Electron uVT validation
=======================

This example is split into two layers on purpose.

Layer 1: quadratic toy model
--------------------------------

Files:

- ``in.electron_uvt``
- ``in.electron_uvt_restart``
- ``draw.ipynb``

These form the LAMMPS-side regression test for classical uVT:

- the generalized coordinate ``Ne`` is integrated correctly,
- ``Ne_dot`` stays coupled to the thermostat chain,
- restart continuity is preserved,
- and the analytic toy-model equilibrium can be checked.

Layer 2: real-system validation
--------------------------------

Directory:

- ``volmer/``

This is a separate template for a real Volmer / PCET-style validation.
It is intentionally kept apart from the toy model so the two test layers
do not get mixed together.

The key contract is still the same:

- ``fix uvt`` consumes ``dedn``
- the actual source of ``dE/dN`` can come from a variable, compute, fix,
  or a model-specific helper

Running
-------

From the LAMMPS root directory:

- ``./build-unified/lmp -in examples/electron-uvt/toy/in.electron_uvt``
- ``./build-unified/lmp -in examples/electron-uvt/toy/in.electron_uvt_restart``

From this directory:

- ``../../../build-unified/lmp -in in.electron_uvt``
- ``../../../build-unified/lmp -in in.electron_uvt_restart``

Run ``in.electron_uvt`` first so that ``in.electron_uvt_restart`` can
read the generated ``uvt.restart`` file.
